\h John
\toc1 John
\mt1 John
\c 3
\p
\v 14 \wj And as Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, so must the Son of Man be lifted up,\wj*
\v 15 \wj that whoever believes in him may have eternal life.\f + \ft Some interpreters hold that the quotation ends at verse 15\f*\wj*
\s1 For God So Loved the World
\p
\v 16 \wj “For God so loved the world,\f + \ft Or For this is how God loved the world\f* that he gave his only Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish but have eternal life.\wj*
\v 17 \wj For God did not send his Son into the world to condemn the world, but in order that the world might be saved through him.\wj*
\v 18 \wj Whoever believes in him is not condemned, but whoever does not believe is condemned already, because he has not believed in the name of the only Son of God.\wj*
\v 19 \wj And this is the judgment: the light has come into the world, and people loved the darkness rather than the light because their works were evil.\wj*
\v 20 \wj For everyone who does wicked things hates the light and does not come to the light, lest his works should be exposed.\wj*
\v 21 \wj But whoever does what is true comes to the light, so that it may be clearly seen that his works have been carried out in God.”\wj*
